# Allowlist for `claude` CLI invocations inside synced shell scripts.
# See .claude/lint-claude-cli-invocations.py — the lint hashes each
# `# claude-cli-invocations:start` / `:end` region and refuses to pass
# if the (hash, path) pair isn't listed here. Adding or rotating an
# entry requires byte-level review of the locked region in the same PR.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated): <sha256>  <path>  <description>
#
# The path field binds each approval to a specific source file —
# copying an allowlisted region into a new synced .sh file does NOT
# inherit the approval; the reviewer has to add a separate entry.

6a803458acd032b7304b57d4a2d3934dd767905fb951cbb60ed970fe6f3e8abd  .claude/skills/agent-loop/scripts/agent-loop.sh  agent-loop.sh: default-worker Claude CLI command builder (--print --permission-mode bypassPermissions, optional --model)
1ba298f3be4a2b302d5a0955ff447df200077f98c613b6f50859f1367641b2a4  .claude/skills/critique/scripts/run-agy-review.sh  run-agy-review.sh: unattended Antigravity reviewer launch (gemini-3.7-flash-high, --effort high, --mode accept-edits, --dangerously-skip-permissions, --add-dir <pinned surface>, --output-format json); --print-timeout is now LOCAL_REVIEW_PASS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (default 1800), clamped to 1-3600 inside the region, with the outer bound at +30s
